# Build context excludes.
#
# The image build needs only:
#   Cargo.toml  Cargo.lock  rust-toolchain.toml
#   crates/  kits/  ui/app/  deploy/healthcheck.sh
#
# Without this file the context is the whole repo, which today carries ~36 GB
# of build artifacts (target/ alone is 32 GB). All of it is sent to the daemon
# on every `docker build .` and invalidates the layer cache on every edit. CI
# never noticed because its checkout is clean — this only bites local builds.

# ── Derived build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
target
crates/notesmith-tauri/target
# Prebuilt desktop sidecar binaries (206 MB). The image compiles its own CLI.
crates/notesmith-tauri/binaries
# Both forms on purpose: `**/` reliably catches the nested ui/app copy, and the
# bare entry covers the context root without depending on whether `**` is read
# as matching zero path segments.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/.svelte-kit
ui/app/build
**/test-results
**/playwright-report

# ── VCS, CI, and OS state ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github
.cargo
**/.DS_Store

# ── Content and docs that are not compiled into the image ────────────────
# kits/ is deliberately NOT listed here: notesmith-kit include_str!s it at
# compile time, and omitting it broke the build once already (fix(container):
# copy kits/ into the image build context).
docs
plans
spikes
mockups
golden-vault
test-fixtures
tools
